# D-105 native (steps/d105-native.md §4; the author's Q39: "сначала в интерпретаторе и потом нативно"): one formal
# reached by two types: `rd2 (Model: m)` gets `o: Other` and `mm: Model` (Model's own, no table), and
# passes each on to `rd`.  The site picks by the value's record: Other's pair table for o, none for mm:
# rd2(o) = 10, rd2(mm) = 1.  Success is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Other:
    size_t: b 20U
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: rd2 (Model: m) size_t
return: rd(m)
fn: go () size_t
    o: merge: Other
    mm: merge: Model
    size_t: x 0U
    x: rd2(mm)
    if: x != 1U
        return: 30U
    return: rd2(o)
size_t: got 0U
got: go()
int: ok 3
if: got = 10U
    ok: 7
if: got = 20U
    ok: 5
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
